  "text": "About Us — Mobile Veterinary Cancer Care\n0\nSkip to Content\nAbout Us\nServices\nLocations\nPet Portal\nFor Veterinarians\nContact Us\nRequest Appointment\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout Us\nServices\nLocations\nPet Portal\nFor Veterinarians\nContact Us\nRequest Appointment\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout Us\nServices\nLocations\nPet Portal\nFor Veterinarians\nContact Us\nRequest Appointment\nOur Mission\nAt Mobile Veterinary Cancer Care we prioritize your pet’s quality of life. We honor our commitment to provide you with the information you need to feel empowered and informed in caring for your pet with cancer.\nChamisa Herrera  DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nDiplomate American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (Oncology)\nDr. Chamisa Herrera is a board certified veterinary oncologist who has been practicing in the Pacific Northwest for the last decade. She is passionate about educating owners following a cancer diagnosis and empowering them with options. Quality of life for pets with cancer is her #1 goal.\nOriginally from rural New Mexico, Dr. Chamisa Herrera fell in love with the Pacific Northwest when she moved to Washington State as a child. When she's not caring for her patients, Dr. Herrera owns a small hobby farm in Bellingham, WA with her wife and 2 young daughters. On the weekends they can be found tending to the farm animals or spending time outdoors. She has three dogs, a cat, a few cows, a couple pigs, and chickens.\nDr. Herrera is also passionate about cancer research. Some of her research projects include investigating mast cell tumors, lung cancer, histiocytic sarcoma, immunomodulation, paraneoplastic syndromes, epigenetics of cancer, and palladia therapy. To learn more, explore some of her\npublished research\n.\nMVCC was founded by Dr. Herrera in 2024 and is independently owned and operated.\nMobile Veterinary Cancer Care\nLocations\nPet Portal\nAbout Us\nServices\nFor Veterinarians\nC\nontact Us",
